@davemorin’s question for @bingfish: games make effort meaningful, and AI promises to remove effort. So what part of life gets worse if an agent wins for you, and what do you deliberately leave in for the human to do?

“Friction is what makes pearls. If you don’t get a sand in the oyster, you just get an oyster.” He adds the qualifier most people skip: sand doesn’t always produce a pearl. It’s just necessary to one.

@brit asks what friction means here. Constraints.

And AI generates its own. “Ten other people are doing the same prompt as you. You’ve got to do something better than them.”

Which raises the bar continuously. “What we now think is great, three years from now we’re going to think of as slop.”

